en.question:
A company gives workers a bonus each month. The bonus comes from the money the company makes:

Up to $100,000 (with $100,000): 20% of this part;
$100,001~$200,000: 15% of this part;
$200,001~$400,000: 10% of this part;
$400,001~$600,000: 5% of this part;
More than $600,001: 3% of this part;

Input the money the company makes this month. Output the bonus.
